tests {
  test("Stubs registered", function() {
    expect(res.getStatus()).to.equal(200);
  });
}

docs {
  Registers the API calls of the HTTP/REST Data source in the WireMock of the API test stack, under
  the path prefix `/dataset-saga-http/`. The stubs carry fixed ids, so a second run replaces them,
  and the metadata `suite`, by which step 15 removes them. A request that no stub matches gets a
  404.

  | Path | Request | Response |
  |---|---|---|
  | `things` | | 200, two Things in the form the FROST port `ThingTree` writes |
  | `missing` | | 404 |
  | `invalid` | | 200, a valid record and a record whose `name` is a number |
  | `pages` | `size` 2, `page` 0, 1, 2 | 200: two, two and one Thing |
  | `cursor-query` | `limit` 1, no `cursor`, `cursor` `abc123`, `def456` | 200: one Thing each |
  | `next-link` | no `page`, then `page` 2 | 200: one Thing each; the first holds a relative link object |
  | `entries` | no `page`, then `page` 2 | 200: two Things in `data`, then one Thing in `data`; the first holds a link in `links.next` |
  | `cursor-header` | no `limit`, no `X-Cursor`, header `X-Cursor` `abc123` | 200: one Thing each |
  | `offset-limit` | `limit` 2, `offset` 80, 82, 84 | 200: two, two and one Thing |
  | `offset` | no `limit`, `offset` 0, 2, 3 | 200: two Things, one Thing, `[]` |
  | `offset-count` | `limit` 1, `offset` 0, 1, 2 | 200: one Thing each; then 404 |

  A cursor response and an `offset-count` response are each one record, so each is one Thing: the
  Data source has one Data structure for all its API calls, and no Mapping comes between the
  source and the sink. A Thing holds the next cursor in `properties.next_cursor`: `abc123` and
  `def456` for `cursor-query`, then none; `abc123` for `cursor-header`, then an empty one. An
  `offset-count` Thing holds the count 1 in `properties.count`. The `entries` API call has the
  path to entries `$.data`, so each element of `data`, or the object in `data`, is one Thing, and
  `links` reaches no Data sink.
}
